## Build 3d: cut LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood.lnlike (cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py) from the measured 41 ms/eval toward the owner's 10 ms target by finishing the h_L=F*h_UL factorization — replacing the current single global cubic spline over ~100 coarse w-nodes with a KINK-AWARE, per-segment interpolation of the smooth channel kernels K_a, so the engine (1F1 double-double ladder, ~0.37 ms/node, the ~85% cost) is evaluated at far fewer nodes. IMPORTANT STEP-RULE NOTE (Professor, authoritative): the brief's '~12 nodes => 7-9 ms' arithmetic is physically wrong. The interpolated object (whether K_a or exact_total) carries ~9 beat-oscillation cycles across the crown wave band [w~0.32, 16.4] (beat frequency = max full-cluster image-delay spread ~3.5), and node count is set by that OSCILLATION CONTENT, not by the kinks. The honest achievable floor for lever A alone is ~15-20 engine nodes => ~13-15 ms (a 2.7-3.2x speedup); a true 6-node/10 ms result is unreachable without either lever B (the 3D surrogate table) or the fenced-out micro-optimizations (nearest-caustic Newton shortcut 1.9->0.3 ms in geometry.py; contraction fusion 2->1 ms in operator.py). Per the owner directive ('do not reach for the heavy table while the cheap structure remains unused') and the Simplifier (lever B's cache/provenance/DATA_CONTRACTS machinery is premature until A is measured), THIS BUILD SHIPS LEVER A ALONE and gates timing at the Professor-derived floor of 15 ms with the derivation recorded, naming the residual levers for a follow-up build. No surrogate table, no lazy cache, no DATA_CONTRACTS artifact, no reduction-exactness/kappa-elimination test are in scope. The engine layer (operator.py, _dd.py, _gauge.py, geometry.py, F_op_grid, all refusal thresholds/messages) is untouched. ASSUMPTION (documented): the OUT-list line 'the 3b node-grid accuracy machinery and its gates' is read as fencing the surrogate/lever-B path, NOT lever A itself — lever A necessarily reworks the node grid, and the brief's own lever-A text says the production interp gate 'moves to the new interpolation scheme's production configuration, tolerance UNCHANGED (1e-3)'.

### WP1: Kink-aware per-segment interpolation of the lensing channel kernels
  What: Rework the coarse-node placement and the kernel interpolation in LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood so the expensive engine (1F1 ladder) is evaluated at a small, deterministic, geometry-derived set of w-nodes and the smooth per-channel kernels K_a are interpolated PER SEGMENT (splines broken exactly at the known regularity boundaries), instead of one global not-a-knot cubic spline over ~100 nodes. This removes the ringing that forced the 100-node grid and cuts the dominant per-eval cost while holding the existing 1e-3 production accuracy gate. Do NOT author tests (Test Developer owns all new tests).
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py — methods LensedRelativeBinningLikelihood._coarse_w_node_grid (line ~721) and _amplification_coefficients (line ~803); module constants block (_DEFAULT_KERNEL_NODES etc., line ~340s). Read-only reference (do not edit): cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/channels.py (_channel_switch, _min_delay_separation, _exact_total, ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate), _gauge.py (exact_transition_channels, smootherstep), operator.py (RHO_START, RHO_END, L_MAX, select_branch, F_op_grid).
  How: SEGMENTED-K_a APPROACH (Simplifier: lean, stays entirely in likelihood.py; no engine boundary change). (1) BREAKPOINTS: in _coarse_w_node_grid, compute the sorted, de-duplicated, in-band (strictly inside (w_min,w_max)) union of: the smootherstep gauge kinks RHO_START/Delta_j and RHO_END/Delta_j for every distinct FULL-CLUSTER pairwise delay separation Delta_j (real images + parked virtual label, exactly the F008 set already assembled here from cluster_delays), PLUS the wave->geometric branch-transition frequency w_branch = max(RHO_END/delta_min, L_MAX/abs(y_prime)), where delta_min is the smallest REAL-channel separation (as in channels._min_delay_separation) and abs(y_prime) is the shear-eigenframe source norm the engine's select_branch/cancellation_exponent uses (compute it the SAME way the engine does — via the mass-sheet map / |y|/sqrt(1-kappa) convention — so the break lands exactly on the engine's per-node branch decision; confirm against operator.cancellation_exponent's definition before coding). Import RHO_START, RHO_END, L_MAX from cogwheel.lensing.chang_refsdal.operator (do not hardcode). (2) SEGMENTS: partition [w_min, w_max] into consecutive segments at those breakpoints. (3) ADAPTIVE PER-SEGMENT NODE BUDGET (accuracy-gated, timing-adaptive): n_seg = clip(ceil(NODES_PER_CYCLE * max_delay_spread * (w_hi - w_lo) / (2*pi)), 4, CAP), where max_delay_spread = the LARGEST full-cluster pairwise delay separation (the fastest beat), NODES_PER_CYCLE ~= 4 (>=3 samples/cycle for a cubic to hold 1e-3), floor 4 (not-a-knot cubic requires >=4 nodes/segment), CAP a documented generous ceiling (e.g. 32) so a pathological narrow-separation config cannot explode the grid. geomspace within each segment; union via np.unique => strictly-increasing positive grid. Node placement is a deterministic function of geometry-only cluster delays + fixed engine thresholds — NEVER error-adaptive. (4) SINGLE BATCHED ENGINE EVAL: evaluate ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate ONCE on the union grid (preserve the Build-3c batched F_op_grid path and its refusal symmetry — do not revert to per-node F_op). (5) PER-SEGMENT INTERPOLATION in _amplification_coefficients: replace the single global CubicSpline over the whole coarse grid with one not-a-knot CubicSpline PER SEGMENT (real and imag parts of partition.kernels separately), each fit only on that segment's coarse nodes, evaluated only on the dense_w sub-samples that fall in that segment (assign each dense point to its owning segment by np.searchsorted on the breakpoints; segment endpoints coincide with breakpoints so this is interpolation, never extrapolation). Breaking the spline exactly at the C2 kink/branch frequencies is the load-bearing change — a single global spline rings there, which is precisely why the old code needed 100 nodes. Keep the per-bin least-squares (k0,k1) reduction (self._kernel_fit_value/_kernel_fit_slope einsums) BYTE-IDENTICAL — only the kernel source changes. (6) REFUSALS: geometry.LensDomainError (macro saddle) and operator.CancellationError (uncertifiable contraction) must still propagate unswallowed so RB and brute paths refuse symmetrically. (7) Update docstrings on both methods and the constants to describe the segmented scheme; reinterpret/rename constants as needed (e.g. introduce _NODES_PER_SEGMENT_CYCLE, _MIN/_MAX_SEGMENT_NODES) but do NOT add a new public constructor kwarg — reuse the existing n_kernel_nodes as an overall cap/hint or leave the signature unchanged (Simplifier: avoid new public API). Guard against degenerate cases: <2 cluster members (no separations) => single unsegmented smooth band with a small default node count; a segment narrower than a few w-eps merged into its neighbour before the >=4-node floor is applied.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: _coarse_w_node_grid returns a deterministic strictly-increasing positive w grid whose total node count on the crown 4-image config is roughly a quarter or less of the former ~100, with segment breakpoints at the in-band full-cluster smootherstep kink frequencies and the wave->geometric branch-transition frequency; _amplification_coefficients interpolates each smooth K_a segment with its OWN not-a-knot cubic spline broken at those breakpoints (no single global spline spanning a kink), evaluates the engine in ONE batched call over the union grid, keeps the (k0,k1) least-squares reduction byte-identical, and lets geometry.LensDomainError and operator.CancellationError propagate unswallowed on both the RB and brute-force paths; RHO_START/RHO_END/L_MAX are imported from operator, not hardcoded; no file in cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/ is modified.
  Max turns: 55

### Professor Inputs
  - CRITICAL arithmetic correction: node count is set by BEAT-OSCILLATION content, not by the kinks. The interpolated kernels carry ~9 oscillation cycles across the crown wave band [w~0.32,16.4] (beat freq = max full-cluster image-delay spread ~3.5), so the honest minimum is ~15-20 engine nodes => ~13-15 ms (2.7-3.2x speedup). The brief's ~12-node/7-9 ms and 6-11 paper-node claims do not apply to the crown band, which lies inside the switch-transition range where K_a carries the oscillatory artificial component.
  - 10 ms is UNREACHABLE with lever A alone. It would require ~6 nodes (<1.5 cycles). The residual levers are: a nearest-caustic Newton shortcut (1.9->0.3 ms, geometry.py, fenced out), a contraction fusion (2->1 ms, operator.py, fenced out), or lever B. Recommendation: gate Build 3d at 15 ms (guaranteed achievable), stretch 12 ms, reserve 10 ms for a follow-up build. -> plan follows the step rule and gates at the 15 ms derived floor.
  - Lever B (3D surrogate table) is NOT needed this build: a 41->15 ms (3x) win is operationally significant, the near-fold regime B targets is rarely the posterior-volume bottleneck, and cheaper paths to the last 3-5 ms exist. -> defer B; no DATA_CONTRACTS artifact / cache / reduction-exactness test in scope.
  - The correct interpolation target is the DELAY-REMOVED per-channel kernel K_a (delays carried analytically by the RB moments), which is C-infinity WITHIN each inter-kink segment; the switch smootherstep is the only source of the C2 kinks. Do NOT interpolate exact_total directly (it oscillates at all image beat frequencies and would need MANY more nodes). MUST break/segment at the wave->geometric branch-transition frequency w_branch=max(RHO_END/delta_min, L_MAX/|y'|) as well, because the geometric branch truncates the asymptotic series at C2 and its 3rd derivative jumps there — do not spline across it.
  - Provided the concrete domain-test specs, tolerances, and 5 anchor configs (crown, near-cusp, well-separated 2-image, near-fold 2-image, sheared small-w macro) that the domain_test_descriptions encode: reconstruction < 5e-4, production null-safe gate 1e-3 unchanged, kink-exactness mutation contrast (>5e-3 for a global spline), RB-vs-brute max(1.5, 1e-2|bf|), and the F009 macro-limit regression must stay green (engine-level, untouched).

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - RECONSTRUCTION ACCURACY vs the exact engine (off-grid probes, per regime). Setup: 5 lens configs anchoring the regimes (Professor): (1) crown 4-image gamma=0.15,kappa=0.05,y=(0.12,0.08); (2) near-cusp 4-image gamma=0.18,kappa=0.03,y=(0.005,0.295); (3) well-separated 2-image gamma=0.10,kappa=0.0,y=(0.8,0.3); (4) near-fold 2-image gamma=0.25,kappa=0.05,y=(0.48,0.0); (5) sheared small-w macro gamma=0.05,kappa=0.02,y=(0.5,0.1); lens mass/redshift giving the crown benchmark band (M_lens~100 Msun, z_lens~0.3; config 5 lighter). Operation: build the new segmented coarse grid, reconstruct the per-channel kernels K_a at 50 OFF-GRID probe w (log-uniform in [w_min,w_max], seeded rng) via the segmented per-kink splines; independently evaluate the TRUE K_a at those 50 probes by calling ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate directly at each probe (full engine, NOT scraped from likelihood internals — cf F010). Expected: null-safe max_a max_w |K_new - K_true| / max_a max_w |K_true| < 5e-4 for every config (half the production gate, leaving margin for the float64 residual-projection reconstruction). Diagnostic: |error| vs w per config; annotate probes above 2e-4.
  - PRODUCTION INTERP NULL-SAFE GATE on the NEW node configuration (tolerance UNCHANGED at 1e-3). Setup: the same 5 configs; the production dense sub-sample grid (kernel_subsamples and n_bins as the shipped likelihood uses). Operation: compute K_a two ways — NEW segmented-spline reconstruction, and REFERENCE = full ChangRefsdalChannels.evaluate at every dense sub-sample. Metric: null-safe max|K_new - K_ref| / max|K_ref| over all channels and frequencies. Expected: < 1e-3 (HARD; the Build-3b gate moved verbatim to the new scheme). Worst regime expected to be the near-fold/near-cusp two-image case (~4e-4 historically).
  - KINK-EXACTNESS CONTRAST / MUTATION (segmentation is load-bearing). Setup: crown config (1); enumerate the in-band full-cluster kink frequencies and the branch-transition frequency; place ~10 probe w within +/-2% of each. Operation: compare (i) the shipped SEGMENTED reconstruction and (ii) a MUTANT that fits a SINGLE GLOBAL not-a-knot cubic spline over the SAME reduced node union (no segmentation) against the REFERENCE dense engine K_a near each kink. Expected: segmented error near kinks < 1e-3 (no degradation at kinks), while the global-spline mutant error near kinks > 5e-3 (>=5x worse) — demonstrating that breaking the spline at the C2 boundaries is necessary at the reduced node count. The mutation must be shown to go genuinely RED (the global spline rings); if it does not, the reduced node count alone was sufficient and the plan's node budget should be re-derived. Independence: build the reference from the engine only, never from the interpolation under test (F002 oracle-tautology guard, AST-guard idiom).
  - RB-vs-BRUTE lnlike AGREEMENT retained (all regimes). Setup: a non-spinning BBH injection (e.g. m1=m2=30 Msun, dL=1 Gpc), zero-noise, single detector, evaluated under each of the 5 lens configs at the reference parameters plus ~10 seeded small perturbations (chirp mass +/-0.5%, eta +/-1%, y1/y2 +/-0.01, M_lens +/-5%). Operation: at every point compute lnlike (new segmented RB path) and lnlike_bruteforce. Expected: |lnlike_RB - lnlike_brute| < max(1.5, 1e-2*|lnlike_brute|) at every point (the existing cogwheel RB tolerance, UNCHANGED). Also assert both paths raise the SAME named error (LensDomainError / CancellationError) on a refused-region probe (refusal symmetry).
  - TIMING GATE — structural-first, absolute ceiling arithmetic-derived (Professor floor 15 ms; step-rule). Setup: crown config (1), warm (>=5 priming lnlike calls), single-thread pinned (OMP/MKL/OPENBLAS/NUMBA_NUM_THREADS=1). PRIMARY (machine-independent) gates, which must lead: (a) engine node count for the crown config reduced by >=4x vs the former 100-node baseline (a deterministic structural assertion on _coarse_w_node_grid output); (b) lnlike_and_metadata faster than lnlike_bruteforce by a conservative speedup floor (e.g. >=2.5x) using the PUBLIC entry points; (c) monotonic sanity — the well-separated 2-image config (3) is not slower than the crown (1). SECONDARY (documented, arithmetic-derived) ceiling: warm best-of-5 min(lnlike) <= 15 ms on the crown config on the pinned reference interpreter, derived as engine(setup~3ms + ~20 nodes*~0.32ms) + contraction~2ms + caustic~1.9ms + non-engine~2.5ms ~= 15 ms (record the measured ms breakdown in the failure message). This 15 ms ceiling is the Professor-certified floor for lever A alone; the 10 ms brief target is NOT gated here and its residual levers (nearest-caustic Newton shortcut and contraction fusion, both fenced out this build; or lever B) are named in SPEC/FINDINGS for a follow-up. Do NOT widen any accuracy tolerance to meet timing.
  - DETERMINISM & GRID VALIDITY of the new node placement. Setup: each of the 5 configs. Operation: call _coarse_w_node_grid twice with identical inputs and assert bit-identical output; assert the grid is strictly increasing, strictly positive, spans exactly [dense_w.min, dense_w.max] at its endpoints (no extrapolation downstream), places a node at each in-band breakpoint, and gives >=4 nodes per segment. Contrast: a config with <2 cluster members (no separations) yields a single smooth unsegmented band. Expected: all assertions hold; node count stays under the documented CAP even for the near-fold small-separation config (delta_min tiny) because the mass-capped w band bounds the beat-oscillation content.

